    "created_at": "2024-03-14T08:09:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-14T08:09:38Z",
    "body": "I think this would be a nice and easy feature to add.\r\n\r\nBefore we commit to implementing it, I want to raise the possibility of returning an object instead of a URL or null.\r\nSomething like `let { url } = URL.parse(input, base);` allows us to add future fields to the return value, such as the error-type, if that's something we would be interested in.\r\n\r\nIn any case, I'm supportive of a non-throwing option to parse URLs.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
