    "updated_at": "2024-03-27T08:13:52Z",
    "body": "Thanks for bringing that to my attention. I don't see the need for parity with `JSON` as we don't try to mimic anything from that API in `URL`. If there was a more widespread pattern of `parse` and `tryParse` methods, maybe, but even then I'd hope we only use the `try` prefix if there's an existing throwing method as it looks rather ungainly.",
